{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to 01d2c5f8, two sentences.\n\n1. The threshold in option (b) is wrong. At 128 uses, the read-publish shell needs 256,474 bytes before births. Each birth adds at most 362 bytes, so (262,144 - 256,474) / 362 gives room for about 15 births. A reserve whose 128 uses span more than about 15 distinct foreign sequences is refused at runtime by entryBytes. With fewer uses there is more room. The lane measures the exact curve before any note states it.\n2. Strike \"and the demo uses that path\". I have not checked whether the demo uses the destination's evidence path. I check it before you rule, if you want that fact."}